# Files EAS Build must not receive.
#
# WHY: the upload was 218 MB. Almost none of it was app code — `docs/screenshots/` alone was 105 MB
# of store captures, and the marketing site is a separate deployment that EAS never builds.
#
# HOW EAS USES THIS FILE — the semantics differ by VCS client, and getting it wrong is dangerous:
#
#   * Git repo (the default here): EAS makes a `git clone --depth 1` of the working copy, then
#     deletes whatever matches this file via `git ls-files --exclude-from`. Because it starts from a
#     clone, .gitignore has ALREADY been applied, so the "everything .gitignore covers" section
#     below is redundant on this path — it matches nothing and costs nothing.
#     Because this repo does not set `requireCommit`, EAS then copies the working directory over
#     that clone so uncommitted and untracked files are included too — and THAT copy step reads
#     only this file, never .gitignore.
#   * Local client (`EAS_NO_VCS=1`): same rule, for everything.
#
# So the "everything .gitignore covers" section below is not redundant belt-and-braces: without it,
# the working-directory copy would carry a stale local /ios and /android (EAS must generate those
# itself with prebuild), any credential file, and dist/. It is NOT needed for node_modules or .git,
# which EAS always ignores when copying regardless of what this file says. Keep it in sync with
# .gitignore.
#
# THE `.git` LINE IS LOAD-BEARING, AND ITS EXACT SPELLING MATTERS. EAS tars the whole shallow clone,
# `.git` included, and `git ls-files` never lists anything inside `.git` — so ignoring a large
# committed file removes only its working copy while its blob stays in the packfile, reclaiming
# about half its weight. EAS's one escape hatch is that it deletes the clone's `.git` outright if
# this file ignores `.git`. It tests the literal path `.git` against these rules, and the `ignore`
# package does not match a bare path against a directory-only pattern:
#
#     .git    ignores('.git') === true     <- what we need
#     .git/   ignores('.git') === false    <- silently keeps the whole packfile
#
# Do not "tidy" the line below by adding a trailing slash.
#
# Measured on this repo: 218 MB originally; 81 MB with the exclusions but a `.git/` typo; ~7 MB
# once `.git` matched. The screenshots were also re-encoded losslessly (105 MB -> 60 MB), which
# still matters — it shrinks any build that does keep history, and the repo itself.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not needed to build the app
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Store captures: used by the marketing site and the store listings, never by
# the app binary. This is the single biggest item in the upload.
docs/screenshots/
# The composed store screens: 49 MB of 1242x2688 PNGs that exist to be uploaded to a store
# console by hand, and are no more part of the app than the captures they are built from.
docs/store-screens/
# Internal notes: a private repo of their own (see .gitignore), never uploaded.
docs/internal/

# The marketing site is its own project with its own dependencies, and deploys from Cloudflare
# Pages' own Git integration — EAS has no reason to see it.
website/

# CI definitions run on GitHub, not on the build worker.
.github/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything .gitignore covers — required only for the `EAS_NO_VCS=1` path (see above), where this
# file is the ONLY filter. Keep in sync with .gitignore.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Deletes the shallow clone's git history from the upload. No trailing slash — see above.
.git

# dependencies
node_modules/

# Expo
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts

# Native
.kotlin/
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision

# EAS credentials (never upload — see docs/RELEASE.md)
credentials.json
google-service-account*.json
play-service-account*.json

# Metro
.metro-health-check*

# debug
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*

# macOS
.DS_Store
*.pem

# local env files
.env*.local

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

# Python bytecode from scripts/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

example

# Generated native folders — EAS runs prebuild itself; uploading a stale local copy makes the build
# use it instead.
/ios
/android

# Playwright MCP scratch output
.playwright-mcp/

# Sentry — the auth token lives in env / EAS secrets, never in a file (see docs/RELEASE.md §11)
sentry.properties
.sentryclirc

# Claude Worktrees
.claude/worktrees/
